WEBVTT

1
00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:25.108
They are an army unlike any other...

2
00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:29.018
crusading across the stars
toward a place called UnderVerse,

3
00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.022
their promised land...

4
00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.389
a constellation of dark new worlds.

5
00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.894
Necromongers, they're called.

6
00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:41.331
And if they cannot convert you,
they will kill you.

7
00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:45.995
Leading them, the Lord Marshal.

8
00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:50.132
He alone has made a pilgrimage
to the gates of the UnderVerse...

9
00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.440
and returned a different being.

10
00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:56.777
Stronger. Stranger.

11
00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.148
Half alive and half...

12
00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.949
something else.

13
00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:17.559
If we are to survive,
a new balance must be found.

14
00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:21.572
In normal times,
evil would be fought by good.

15
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.632
But in times like these, well,

16
00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.873
it should be fought
by another kind of evil.

17
00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:06.250
Linin' him up for you. Port-side shot comin' up.
Steady. Here we go.

18
00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:16.290
Steady.

19
00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.388
Take it. Take it!

20
00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.899
Take the shot!

21
00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.631
Shit!
Toombs, we're runnin' out of road!

22
00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:28.900
Shut up! I got it! Again!

23
00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:34.241
Now!

24
00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:36.440
Toombs!

25
00:03:50.662 --> 00:03:54.120
Riddick.

26
00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:58.264
I don't know, Toombs.
Looks kinda tight.

27
00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:01.966
Not where I'm sittin'.
This is the biggest payday ever,

28
00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:05.101
So throw on a fresh pair of panties.
Let's get this right.

29
00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:19.923
Three meters clearance port-side.
One and a half meters starboard.

30
00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.483
We got a choke point comin' up.

31
00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.532
What the shit was that?

32
00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:42.506
Tags, you got eyes on Riddick?

33
00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:45.379
Tags?

34
00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:51.445
Jesus.

35
00:04:51.523 --> 00:04:54.458
He just ghosted two guys,
and I never even saw him.

36
00:04:56.128 --> 00:05:00.064
What do you think, Toombs? I mean, maybe we oughta just...
I think you're my new gunner.

37
00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:02.123
Grab a Gat.

38
00:05:09.641 --> 00:05:11.700
Stay on top of him this time.

39
00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:43.268
You made three mistakes.

40
00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:48.303
First, you took the job.

41
00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.405
Second, you came light.

42
00:05:50.482 --> 00:05:55.078
A four-man crew for me?
Fuckin' insulting.

43
00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.282
But the worst mistake you made...

44
00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.320
Empty gun rack.

45
00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:10.068
- What's the bounty on my head?
- One mil.

46
00:06:12.804 --> 00:06:17.434
- One-point-five.
- What slam pays 1.5 for a convict?

47
00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:19.773
Private party.

48
00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:22.780
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Guy, guy! Easy! Anonymous.

49
00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:26.215
- That's what the sheet said.
- What planet?

50
00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:29.554
Helion Prime.

51
00:06:36.828 --> 00:06:39.763
Whoa. Where you goin'?
Last question.

52
00:06:39.831 --> 00:06:43.494
And you better get this one right, merc.

53
00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.469
Whose ship is this?

54
00:06:45.537 --> 00:06:48.233
Mine?

55
00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.828
Knew they'd come for me.

56
00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.888
Took 'em five years, but I knew.

57
00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:18.630
You don't expect these mercs
to have any honor, any code.

58
00:07:20.405 --> 00:07:24.774
But this new bounty from a holy man,

59
00:07:24.843 --> 00:07:27.812
a guy whose neck I saved...

60
00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:31.215
Well, lesson learned.

61
00:07:31.283 --> 00:07:34.013
No such word as "friend."

62
00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:37.317
Can only end bad
when you let someone get too close.

63
00:07:38.523 --> 00:07:40.718
Bad for them.

64
00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:48.832
So now it's back to all the brightness...
and everything I hate.

65
00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:52.734
Wonder if she'll be there.

66
00:08:02.547 --> 00:08:07.541
Act like an animal and I'm gonna slot you up like one.
This one is always in trouble.

67
00:08:07.619 --> 00:08:09.587
I knew it!
I smell it.

68
00:08:30.642 --> 00:08:32.337
Get in there!

69
00:08:58.103 --> 00:09:00.094
Can we shut the goddamn noise?

70
00:09:32.504 --> 00:09:36.406
They say most of your
brain shuts down in cryosleep.

71
00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:40.002
Brain shuts down in cryosleep.

72
00:09:40.078 --> 00:09:43.275
- All but the primitive side.
- All but the primitive side.

73
00:09:43.348 --> 00:09:45.646
The animal side.

74
00:09:45.717 --> 00:09:49.244
All but the Furyan side.

75
00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:58.726
Some of us still remember the true
crime that happened here on Furya.

76
00:10:01.566 --> 00:10:04.228
And once you wake...

77
00:10:04.302 --> 00:10:07.066
truly wake...

78
00:10:09.474 --> 00:10:11.704
you'll remember too.

79
00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:20.014
Helion Prime is on alert condition four.

80
00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:29.852
Unrecognized craft. You need to follow me
to Spaceport Six for security inspections.

81
00:10:29.928 --> 00:10:33.159
Hey! Do you hear me?

82
00:10:33.231 --> 00:10:35.893
Follow me to Spaceport Six now!

83
00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.283
Imam, pray for us.

84
00:11:28.353 --> 00:11:31.618
It was confirmed
two seasons back. Yes.

85
00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:34.022
They're coming here.
I mean, are we next?

86
00:11:34.092 --> 00:11:36.083
Militants storm...

87
00:11:36.161 --> 00:11:39.289
Yes. But going to the
underground shelters if it happens...

88
00:11:39.364 --> 00:11:41.559
You're right.
That's what I thought too.

89
00:11:41.633 --> 00:11:44.101
Are you staying or leaving?

90
00:11:44.169 --> 00:11:46.501
It's the end of everything.
Everything!

91
00:11:46.571 --> 00:11:50.063
- Well, my neighbors...
- Half my street is gone.

92
00:11:50.141 --> 00:11:52.061
What are we gonna do?
I don't know. I don't know.

93
00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:54.070
Hood of the devil.
That's what someone called 'em.

94
00:11:54.112 --> 00:11:56.205
Them? Who is them?
Some kind of new creature...

95
00:11:56.281 --> 00:11:58.272
This is nonsense.
It's all nonsense.

96
00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:02.252
So tall that it touches the clouds.

97
00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:06.689
And there's nothing around this
statue, this colossus. Nothing left.

98
00:12:06.758 --> 00:12:08.988
It's their calling card.

99
00:12:19.471 --> 00:12:22.668
Did you know all your doors were locked?

100
00:12:27.746 --> 00:12:30.112
Five years ago,

101
00:12:30.181 --> 00:12:33.082
I took two people off that planet...

102
00:12:33.151 --> 00:12:37.383
A kid, Jack,
who everyone else thought was a boy,

103
00:12:37.455 --> 00:12:40.151
and a holy man...

104
00:12:40.225 --> 00:12:42.159
searching for New Mecca.

105
00:12:45.697 --> 00:12:47.790
Your wife...

106
00:12:49.701 --> 00:12:51.692
She's in the shower.

107
00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:56.730
I told one man...

108
00:12:56.808 --> 00:12:59.971
where I might go.

109
00:13:00.045 --> 00:13:03.981
I showed trust to one man.

110
00:13:04.049 --> 00:13:07.541
Did I make a mistake, Imam?

111
00:13:07.619 --> 00:13:09.951
There is no simple answer.

112
00:13:10.021 --> 00:13:14.720
Whatever was said
was meant to give us a chance...

113
00:13:14.793 --> 00:13:16.784
a fighting chance.

114
00:13:18.196 --> 00:13:21.529
Were it not for the threat of invasion,
I never would have betrayed you.

115
00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.831
I give you my word, Riddick.
Riddick!

116
00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.861
Riddick!

117
00:13:30.775 --> 00:13:33.300
And a daughter...

118
00:13:34.746 --> 00:13:37.840
- No!
- Whose name would be...

119
00:13:37.916 --> 00:13:40.476
If you have issue with me,
you let it be with me.

120
00:13:40.552 --> 00:13:43.020
- You need not know their names.
- Ziza.

121
00:13:45.256 --> 00:13:47.156
My name is Ziza.

122
00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.394
Ziza.

123
00:13:52.097 --> 00:13:56.090
- Cute kid.
- Did you really kill monsters?

124
00:13:56.167 --> 00:13:58.692
The ones that were gonna
hurt my father?

125
00:14:00.538 --> 00:14:02.665
Such are our bedtime stories.

126
00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:05.437
Go, Ziza. Go on!

127
00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:14.612
So now who do I have to kill
to get this payday off my head?

128
00:14:30.502 --> 00:14:35.030
It is said the comet
always precedes them...

129
00:14:35.106 --> 00:14:37.597
these world-enders.

130
00:14:39.678 --> 00:14:41.612
The Coalsack planets are gone.

131
00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:44.513
Eight million settlers missing.

132
00:14:44.582 --> 00:14:48.211
The entire Aquilan System is gone too.

133
00:14:48.286 --> 00:14:52.689
Helion Prime shares its sunlight
with all worlds nearby.

134
00:14:54.826 --> 00:14:59.525
If we fall, they fall.

135
00:14:59.597 --> 00:15:01.929
And after that...

136
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.163
My God,
how do I save my family?

137
00:15:09.541 --> 00:15:12.339
Have you heard anything I've said?

138
00:15:14.646 --> 00:15:18.275
You said it's all circling the drain...
the whole universe.

139
00:15:18.349 --> 00:15:20.283
Right?
That's right.

140
00:15:29.294 --> 00:15:31.455
Had to end sometime.

141
00:15:49.047 --> 00:15:51.038
The one you want is now here.

142
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.434
And whose throat is this?

143
00:16:12.437 --> 00:16:17.101
If you cut my throat, I'll not be able to
rescind the offer that brought you here.

144
00:16:17.175 --> 00:16:19.700
Nor tell you why it's so vital
that you did come.

145
00:16:19.778 --> 00:16:22.679
The blade comes off
when the bounty comes off.

146
00:16:22.747 --> 00:16:26.376
This is Aereon,
an envoy from the Elemental race.

147
00:16:26.451 --> 00:16:28.817
She means you no harm.

148
00:16:32.724 --> 00:16:36.387
There are very few of us who have met a
Necromonger and lived to speak of it.

149
00:16:36.461 --> 00:16:41.091
So when I choose to speak of it,
you should choose to listen.

150
00:16:41.166 --> 00:16:43.225
Necromonger.

151
00:16:43.301 --> 00:16:48.603
It is the name that will convert
or kill every last human life...

152
00:16:48.673 --> 00:16:51.767
unless the universe
can rebalance itself.

153
00:16:53.711 --> 00:16:58.080
Maybe you should pretend like you're talkin'
to someone educated in the penal system.

154
00:16:58.149 --> 00:17:01.346
In fact, don't pretend.

155
00:17:01.419 --> 00:17:04.786
Balance is everything
to elementals.

156
00:17:04.856 --> 00:17:06.847
Water to fire.
Earth to air.

157
00:17:06.925 --> 00:17:09.257
We have 33 different words for it.

158
00:17:09.327 --> 00:17:13.923
But now we have only time
to speak of the balance of opposites.

159
00:17:13.998 --> 00:17:17.866
There is a story, Riddick,
of young male Furyans...

160
00:17:17.936 --> 00:17:20.461
strangled at birth...

161
00:17:20.538 --> 00:17:22.733
strangled with their own cords.

162
00:17:24.409 --> 00:17:27.105
When Aereon told this story
to the Helion leaders,

163
00:17:27.178 --> 00:17:29.271
I told her of you.

164
00:17:29.347 --> 00:17:32.441
- What do you know of your early years?
- Do you remember your home world?

165
00:17:32.517 --> 00:17:34.985
- Where it was?
- Have you met any others?

166
00:17:35.053 --> 00:17:37.044
Others like yourself.

167
00:17:39.691 --> 00:17:43.718
Sister, they don't know what
to do with just one of me.

168
00:17:43.795 --> 00:17:46.286
Open up in there!

169
00:17:46.364 --> 00:17:48.764
- Stand back!
- Open up!

170
00:17:48.833 --> 00:17:50.767
They are searching houses!
Shh!

171
00:17:50.835 --> 00:17:53.827
They look for a man who came here today.
They think he might be a spy.

172
00:17:53.905 --> 00:17:56.237
A spy? Did someone see
him come here today?

173
00:17:56.307 --> 00:17:57.968
Did they?
Lajjun, stop!

174
00:17:58.042 --> 00:18:02.604
We're sure he's in there! I will send them away.
But wait one minute, please.

175
00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.843
Will you wait one minute
to save worlds?

176
00:18:07.552 --> 00:18:10.282
Not my fight.

177
00:18:10.355 --> 00:18:12.619
So, you will leave us
to our fate,

178
00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.022
just like you did her.

179
00:18:15.093 --> 00:18:18.324
Break it down!

180
00:18:20.098 --> 00:18:21.156
Get him!

181
00:18:21.232 --> 00:18:23.564
Come. Let us try to send them away.

182
00:18:27.038 --> 00:18:29.268
- Move it. Come on.
- Leave us alone!

183
00:18:31.509 --> 00:18:34.910
There is no one here!

184
00:18:34.979 --> 00:18:38.779
You don't understand. He can help us!
He can help us!

185
00:18:41.986 --> 00:18:43.977
Go!

186
00:18:49.327 --> 00:18:52.296
You're not afraid of the dark, are you?

187
00:19:12.684 --> 00:19:15.244
- Get him!
- Where is he?

188
00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.652
In there!

189
00:19:44.615 --> 00:19:47.106
You mentioned her.

190
00:19:47.185 --> 00:19:50.052
She, uh...

191
00:19:50.121 --> 00:19:52.055
She went looking for you.

192
00:19:52.123 --> 00:19:55.524
People died.
She went to prison.

193
00:19:55.593 --> 00:19:59.427
I... I don't remember where.

194
00:20:00.431 --> 00:20:05.869
But it was a world so hot
you not survive on the surface.

195
00:20:05.937 --> 00:20:09.429
Crematoria.
Young Jack.

196
00:20:09.507 --> 00:20:11.702
She thought of you
as her older brother.

197
00:20:11.776 --> 00:20:14.802
She worshipped you.
You were supposed to watch her.

198
00:20:15.947 --> 00:20:18.609
She never forgave you...

199
00:20:18.683 --> 00:20:22.050
for leaving just when
she needed you most.

200
00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:27.217
She needed to stay away from me.
You all do.

201
00:20:29.494 --> 00:20:31.962
Riddick.

202
00:20:33.698 --> 00:20:37.099
Are you gonna stop
the new monsters now?

203
00:20:50.048 --> 00:20:53.848
Furyans.
Defiant to the end.

204
00:21:31.622 --> 00:21:33.556
No, no.

205
00:21:33.624 --> 00:21:36.115
We go to the shelter.

206
00:21:36.194 --> 00:21:38.662
We take only ourselves.

207
00:21:59.817 --> 00:22:01.808
Stay close.

208
00:22:34.318 --> 00:22:36.878
No!

209
00:23:48.059 --> 00:23:50.687
Flight leaders, get all
squads off the ground now.

210
00:23:50.761 --> 00:23:53.594
We have heavy inbound.

211
00:23:54.699 --> 00:23:56.826
Follow me in!

212
00:24:15.052 --> 00:24:17.213
The next shelter.
This way!

213
00:24:17.288 --> 00:24:19.313
Yeah!

214
00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:21.756
Whoo-hoo!

215
00:24:42.813 --> 00:24:46.010
I'll see if it's safe.

216
00:24:51.222 --> 00:24:54.749
- Stay back!
- Come, Ziza.

217
00:25:12.576 --> 00:25:14.908
Come!

218
00:25:34.432 --> 00:25:36.457
You following me?

219
00:26:14.004 --> 00:26:16.063
Lajjun and Ziza!

220
00:26:16.140 --> 00:26:18.836
When it's over. Let me go.
I must get to my family!

221
00:26:18.909 --> 00:26:21.241
When it's over.

222
00:26:47.605 --> 00:26:49.766
I borrowed a ship.

223
00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:53.435
You can ride along,
if you don't mind riding with a convict.

224
00:26:53.511 --> 00:26:56.844
I thank you, but I must get
my family across the river.

225
00:26:56.914 --> 00:26:59.178
God willing, there is still
a shelter I can get them...

226
00:26:59.250 --> 00:27:01.275
I'm sure God has his tricks,

227
00:27:01.352 --> 00:27:05.118
but getting out of places
no one else can,

228
00:27:05.189 --> 00:27:07.384
that's one of mine.

229
00:27:08.392 --> 00:27:10.451
Let's get your family.

230
00:27:13.063 --> 00:27:15.054
Aah!

231
00:27:44.595 --> 00:27:46.586
In here.

232
00:27:47.731 --> 00:27:50.097
Get in.

233
00:27:51.802 --> 00:27:53.997
Shh.

234
00:28:58.202 --> 00:29:00.796
- Imam!
- Don't follow me.

235
00:30:35.499 --> 00:30:38.332
There will be
an afterlife for me.

236
00:30:40.004 --> 00:30:41.938
Will there be for you?

237
00:31:59.883 --> 00:32:03.410
Let's go replenish the ranks.

238
00:32:16.266 --> 00:32:18.700
Never fails to inspire, does it?

239
00:32:18.769 --> 00:32:20.999
Each time a dynasty falls.

240
00:32:21.071 --> 00:32:24.598
Remember your place,
Dame Vaako.

241
00:32:24.675 --> 00:32:27.803
My place is at your side,
dear husband.

242
00:32:27.878 --> 00:32:30.005
From here till UnderVerse come.

243
00:32:54.438 --> 00:32:57.703
In this 'verse,

244
00:32:57.775 --> 00:33:01.836
life is antagonistic
to the natural state.

245
00:33:03.380 --> 00:33:08.443
Here, humans in all
their various races...

246
00:33:08.519 --> 00:33:11.647
are a spontaneous outbreak...

247
00:33:11.722 --> 00:33:13.917
an unguided mistake.

248
00:33:13.991 --> 00:33:15.982
Our purpose...

249
00:33:16.059 --> 00:33:19.893
is to correct that mistake.

250
00:33:21.098 --> 00:33:24.397
Because there is another 'verse...

251
00:33:24.468 --> 00:33:29.462
a 'verse where life
is welcomed and cherished.

252
00:33:29.540 --> 00:33:35.342
A ravishing, ever-new place
called UnderVerse.

253
00:33:36.580 --> 00:33:40.277
But the road to that 'verse...

254
00:33:40.350 --> 00:33:42.341
crosses over the threshold.

255
00:33:42.419 --> 00:33:45.513
Threshold!
Take us to the threshold!

256
00:33:45.589 --> 00:33:49.389
What you call... death.

257
00:33:49.459 --> 00:33:55.261
So it is this 'verse
that must be cleansed of life,

258
00:33:55.332 --> 00:33:59.598
so that UnderVerse
can populate and prosper.

259
00:34:02.172 --> 00:34:06.734
Look around you.
Every Necromonger in this hall,

260
00:34:06.810 --> 00:34:11.270
every one of the Legion Vast that just
swept aside your defenses in one night...

261
00:34:11.348 --> 00:34:14.078
was once like you.

262
00:34:14.151 --> 00:34:16.881
Fought as feebly as you.

263
00:34:17.955 --> 00:34:20.890
Every Necromonger
that lives today...

264
00:34:20.958 --> 00:34:23.085
is a convert.

265
00:34:23.160 --> 00:34:28.359
- There'll be no conversions!
- We all began as something else!

266
00:34:30.634 --> 00:34:35.071
It was hard for me to accept, too,
when I first heard these words.

267
00:34:35.138 --> 00:34:37.732
But I changed.

268
00:34:37.808 --> 00:34:40.140
I let them take away my pain.

269
00:34:40.210 --> 00:34:44.408
- You betrayed your faith!
- Just as you will change...

270
00:34:44.481 --> 00:34:49.942
when you realize that the threshold
to the UnderVerse will be crossed...

271
00:34:50.020 --> 00:34:54.184
only by those who have
embraced the Necromonger faith.

272
00:34:54.258 --> 00:34:57.386
For those of you
who will right now...

273
00:34:57.461 --> 00:35:01.522
drop to your knees
and ask to be purified.

274
00:35:01.598 --> 00:35:05.125
We will not renounce our faith!
No one here will do what you ask.

275
00:35:06.570 --> 00:35:08.003
It is unthinkable!

276
00:35:08.071 --> 00:35:13.441
This is a world of many peoples,
many religions!

277
00:35:13.510 --> 00:35:17.913
And we simply cannot
and will not be converted!

278
00:35:17.981 --> 00:35:20.779
Then I'll take your soul.

279
00:35:32.129 --> 00:35:34.689
Join him...

280
00:35:34.765 --> 00:35:37.962
or join me.

281
00:35:57.888 --> 00:36:00.550
This is your one chance.

282
00:36:00.624 --> 00:36:03.092
Take the Lord Marshal's offer
and bow.

283
00:36:03.160 --> 00:36:05.993
I bow to no man.

284
00:36:13.170 --> 00:36:15.195
He's not a man.

285
00:36:15.272 --> 00:36:18.935
He's the holy Half-Dead
who has seen the UnderVerse.

286
00:36:19.009 --> 00:36:21.500
Look, I'm not
with everyone here.

287
00:36:21.578 --> 00:36:24.172
But I will take a piece of him.

288
00:36:30.754 --> 00:36:32.745
A piece you will have.

289
00:37:00.751 --> 00:37:02.776
Stop him!

290
00:37:15.198 --> 00:37:17.632
Irgun. One of my best.

291
00:37:17.701 --> 00:37:20.169
If you say so.

292
00:37:23.874 --> 00:37:26.138
What do you think of this blade?

293
00:37:35.886 --> 00:37:38.252
I think it's a half-gram heavy
on the back end.

294
00:37:38.321 --> 00:37:40.289
In our faith,

295
00:37:40.357 --> 00:37:42.518
you keep what you kill.

296
00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:51.859
Are you familiar to me?

297
00:37:54.704 --> 00:37:58.196
Have we met
on some distant field?

298
00:37:59.376 --> 00:38:01.105
You'd think I'd remember.

299
00:38:02.646 --> 00:38:05.911
You'd think I would too.

300
00:38:05.982 --> 00:38:09.543
Take him before the Quasi-Deads.

301
00:38:16.526 --> 00:38:19.893
Perhaps the breeder
would do it...

302
00:38:19.963 --> 00:38:22.454
if somebody just asked him.

303
00:38:24.434 --> 00:38:26.834
It is a rare offer.

304
00:38:28.738 --> 00:38:31.707
A visit inside Necropolis.

305
00:38:33.310 --> 00:38:37.007
It's been a long time
since I smelled beautiful.

306
00:38:38.815 --> 00:38:40.942
Let me show you the way.

307
00:39:34.571 --> 00:39:36.903
Beautiful eyes.

308
00:39:36.973 --> 00:39:38.964
Come.

309
00:39:41.711 --> 00:39:45.807
The last six Lord Marshals
have called this home.

310
00:39:45.882 --> 00:39:48.146
Magnificent, isn't it?

311
00:39:48.218 --> 00:39:51.984
I might have gone a different way.
True of us all.

312
00:39:53.990 --> 00:39:58.086
Converts receiving the mark
of the Necromonger.

313
00:40:00.330 --> 00:40:03.595
They learn how one pain
can lessen another.

314
00:40:17.714 --> 00:40:19.705
There now.

315
00:40:21.384 --> 00:40:24.683
That is just... perfect.

316
00:40:28.058 --> 00:40:31.255
The more you resist them,

317
00:40:31.328 --> 00:40:33.694
the greater the damage will be.

318
00:40:36.266 --> 00:40:39.292
A new one.

319
00:40:39.369 --> 00:40:42.167
You've brought us the one.

320
00:40:55.719 --> 00:40:58.449
Interesting breeder.

321
00:41:14.504 --> 00:41:17.132
Making entry.

322
00:41:17.207 --> 00:41:20.973
This won't take long.

323
00:41:21.044 --> 00:41:24.104
We've entered his neocortex.

324
00:41:24.180 --> 00:41:28.048
- Ahh! The Riddick!
- Regress.

325
00:41:28.118 --> 00:41:31.747
Scanning fresh memories.

326
00:41:31.821 --> 00:41:34.847
Thoughts of someone called Jack.

327
00:41:34.924 --> 00:41:36.824
Riddick!

328
00:41:38.695 --> 00:41:40.754
She went to prison.

329
00:41:41.898 --> 00:41:44.924
Now we find thoughts of an Elemental.

330
00:41:45.001 --> 00:41:48.164
The one race that would slow
the spread of Necromongers.

331
00:41:48.238 --> 00:41:50.502
- Furyans.
- Furyans.

332
00:41:55.845 --> 00:41:58.006
Where does he come from?

333
00:41:58.081 --> 00:42:02.575
Who are his people?
These are the things I need to know.

334
00:42:04.554 --> 00:42:07.455
We find energy.

335
00:42:08.792 --> 00:42:11.625
You must settle your past.

336
00:42:11.695 --> 00:42:16.655
We find Furyan energy.

337
00:42:16.733 --> 00:42:19.065
- For all of us.
- He's Furyan!

338
00:42:20.503 --> 00:42:22.596
Furyan!

339
00:42:24.274 --> 00:42:26.936
A Furyan survivor!

340
00:42:28.211 --> 00:42:33.945
Look at our world, at the graves
of those who didn't escape 30 years ago.

341
00:42:34.017 --> 00:42:36.485
There is no future
until we settle our past...

342
00:42:39.055 --> 00:42:42.115
for all of us
who bear the mark.

343
00:42:43.159 --> 00:42:45.957
Kill the Furyan! Kill the Riddick!

344
00:42:46.029 --> 00:42:48.998
Kill the Riddick! Kill the Riddick!
Kill the Riddick!

345
00:42:49.065 --> 00:42:51.260
Kill the Riddick!
Kill the Riddick.

346
00:43:25.502 --> 00:43:27.333
Who is this man?

347
00:43:29.205 --> 00:43:32.174
Find him. Whatever it takes. Find him!

348
00:44:06.976 --> 00:44:11.970
Let me guess.
A five-man crew this time.

349
00:44:12.048 --> 00:44:14.346
Couple of things
you could have done better.

350
00:44:18.688 --> 00:44:23.318
First, trash the locator beacon
inside my ship... the one you jacked.

351
00:44:23.393 --> 00:44:26.760
And second... and this is really
the more important part...

352
00:44:26.830 --> 00:44:30.061
dust my dick
when you get the chance.

353
00:44:30.133 --> 00:44:33.864
- Any questions?
- Yeah.

354
00:44:36.406 --> 00:44:38.033
What took you so long?

355
00:44:45.348 --> 00:44:47.578
Let's go, big boy.

356
00:45:00.263 --> 00:45:04.597
In and out, unsuspected and undetected.
Damn, I love a good smash-and-grab.

357
00:45:04.667 --> 00:45:07.227
Not so fast. Not so fast.

358
00:45:07.303 --> 00:45:09.737
Dickheads.
We're pickin' up fields here.

359
00:45:09.806 --> 00:45:12.741
Unknown fields detected on hull.

360
00:45:12.809 --> 00:45:16.336
I knew it. Here it comes.
This is some kind of scan.

361
00:45:16.412 --> 00:45:18.403
I don't know.
Readin' our Btus, maybe?

362
00:45:18.481 --> 00:45:21.973
- Let's drop one.
- Dropping.

363
00:45:29.993 --> 00:45:31.984
Decoy launched.

364
00:45:37.800 --> 00:45:40.769
Preparing
to engage ion drive. So,

365
00:45:40.837 --> 00:45:44.739
where do we drop
your merc-killin' ass?

366
00:45:44.807 --> 00:45:47.139
Who's gonna pay
the most for you now?

367
00:45:47.210 --> 00:45:50.941
- Butcher Bay?
- Butcher Bay.

368
00:45:51.014 --> 00:45:53.778
Ten minutes every other day
on the dog run.

369
00:45:53.850 --> 00:45:56.819
Protein waffles aren't bad.

370
00:45:56.886 --> 00:46:00.754
Hey, how 'bout Ursa Luna?
Nice little double-max prison.

371
00:46:00.823 --> 00:46:05.226
They keep a cell open for me...
just in case I drop in.

372
00:46:05.295 --> 00:46:07.229
You know the problem
with these joints now?

373
00:46:07.297 --> 00:46:10.266
Health clubs
for waffle-eatin' pussies.

374
00:46:10.333 --> 00:46:13.063
Maybe we should think about
uppin' our game here a little bit.

375
00:46:13.136 --> 00:46:15.502
Think about someplace
truly diabolical.

376
00:46:15.572 --> 00:46:17.563
What the hell is he thinkin' now?

377
00:46:17.640 --> 00:46:20.165
He's thinkin' a triple-max prison.

378
00:46:20.243 --> 00:46:23.610
A no-daylight slam.
Only three of 'em left in this system...

379
00:46:23.680 --> 00:46:28.014
two of 'em outta range for a shitty little
undercutter like this one with no legs.

380
00:46:28.084 --> 00:46:31.611
Leavin' just... one...

381
00:46:31.688 --> 00:46:34.623
Crematoria.

382
00:46:34.691 --> 00:46:37.489
That is what you had in mind,
right, Toombs?

383
00:46:37.560 --> 00:46:41.189
- Hey, how does he know where we're goin', and we don't?
- Dope it out.

384
00:46:41.264 --> 00:46:44.028
- I hate this run.
- Just do it!

385
00:46:44.100 --> 00:46:46.762
Don't know about this
new crew of yours.

386
00:46:46.836 --> 00:46:50.169
They seem a bit skittish.

387
00:46:50.239 --> 00:46:53.766
Probably shouldn't tell 'em
what happened to the last crew.

388
00:47:01.484 --> 00:47:05.978
You know, you supposed
to be some slick-shit killer.

389
00:47:06.055 --> 00:47:08.580
Now look at you...

390
00:47:08.658 --> 00:47:11.821
all back-of-the-bus
and shit.

391
00:47:48.398 --> 00:47:51.060
I say we attack Helion Two next.

392
00:47:51.134 --> 00:47:53.068
Take it straight
into their teeth.

393
00:47:53.136 --> 00:47:56.537
It'll cost you 20,000 heads, five warrior ships.
Nothing more, I swear it.

394
00:47:56.606 --> 00:47:59.939
While I do prize brute force,

395
00:48:00.009 --> 00:48:03.137
this approach
is perhaps more artful.

396
00:48:03.212 --> 00:48:06.045
Start at the end.

397
00:48:06.115 --> 00:48:08.106
Go straight to Helion Five,

398
00:48:08.184 --> 00:48:10.379
the last planet in the system.

399
00:48:10.453 --> 00:48:13.081
We approach from the night side.

400
00:48:13.156 --> 00:48:16.125
Remove these cannon first,

401
00:48:16.192 --> 00:48:19.025
then attack
the larger placements at speed.

402
00:48:19.095 --> 00:48:21.893
We'll catch them on their rear flank.
And in ten days’ time,

403
00:48:21.964 --> 00:48:26.298
the rest of those worlds
will tumble before us.

404
00:48:26.369 --> 00:48:28.701
You see, as with most,
their blind spot...

405
00:48:28.771 --> 00:48:31.069
is right behind them.

406
00:48:33.142 --> 00:48:36.703
I've located an ion trail
which leads off-world.

407
00:48:36.779 --> 00:48:39.475
Then you should be
off-world, Vaako.

408
00:48:39.549 --> 00:48:42.143
I've deployed a tracker team.
One of the best.

409
00:48:42.218 --> 00:48:45.949
Wherever Riddick has gone,
you lens him out and cleanse him.

410
00:48:46.956 --> 00:48:50.915
- You.
- You want me to take a frigate for one breeder?

411
00:48:50.993 --> 00:48:53.052
Don't question it, Vaako!

412
00:48:54.964 --> 00:48:58.161
Take it on faith.

413
00:49:01.337 --> 00:49:04.738
He's always been unsettled around you...

414
00:49:04.807 --> 00:49:06.832
the Lord Marshal.

415
00:49:06.909 --> 00:49:09.810
Unsteady.

416
00:49:09.879 --> 00:49:13.542
Perhaps because he knows
he's half the warrior you are.

417
00:49:13.616 --> 00:49:16.676
Some say he's too artistic
for the job.

418
00:49:18.187 --> 00:49:20.815
I wouldn't be surprised
if someone promoted him soon...

419
00:49:20.890 --> 00:49:23.825
to full dead.

420
00:49:26.229 --> 00:49:28.163
Take care what you say.

421
00:49:28.231 --> 00:49:31.132
Should I say it softly?

422
00:49:31.200 --> 00:49:34.169
So it sounds more
like conspiracy?

423
00:49:34.237 --> 00:49:38.071
Oh, why is it that when anyone breathes
about the demise of him on the throne...

424
00:49:38.141 --> 00:49:40.803
everyone assumes a conspiracy?

425
00:49:42.512 --> 00:49:45.879
Why isn't that
just prudent planning?

426
00:49:45.948 --> 00:49:48.473
When he is ready,
he will name a successor.

427
00:49:48.551 --> 00:49:50.644
Who?

428
00:49:50.720 --> 00:49:54.986
Toal? Scales? The Purifier?

429
00:49:55.057 --> 00:49:57.389
None of them...

430
00:49:57.460 --> 00:50:00.224
with the strength, the dignity,

431
00:50:00.296 --> 00:50:04.392
of Lord Vaako.

432
00:50:04.467 --> 00:50:06.697
You can keep what you kill.

433
00:50:06.769 --> 00:50:10.034
- Stop.
- That is the Necromonger way.

434
00:50:10.106 --> 00:50:13.667
I said... stop.

435
00:50:13.743 --> 00:50:17.110
His death will come in due time
and not a moment sooner.

436
00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:20.775
- Why? - Because I serve him. We all serve him.
It's called fidelity.

437
00:50:20.850 --> 00:50:23.011
It's called stupidity.

438
00:50:32.094 --> 00:50:34.085
Well, finally some attention.

439
00:50:47.009 --> 00:50:50.877
You have such greatness in you.

440
00:50:50.947 --> 00:50:53.074
If only you could see it like I do.

441
00:50:55.952 --> 00:50:57.977
You know what I want?

442
00:50:59.622 --> 00:51:03.649
Today I came up behind him
in perfect silence and he knew.

443
00:51:03.726 --> 00:51:06.160
I wanna go down in Necropolis.

444
00:51:08.064 --> 00:51:10.055
Right now.

445
00:51:10.132 --> 00:51:15.160
His half-dead soul sensed I was
behind him. He sees everything.

446
00:51:15.238 --> 00:51:17.433
When no one is looking...

447
00:51:17.506 --> 00:51:20.066
when no one's around...

448
00:51:20.142 --> 00:51:22.406
I'm gonna get down on my knees...

449
00:51:24.146 --> 00:51:27.582
while you sit on the throne.

450
00:51:49.805 --> 00:51:53.639
- How unexpected.
- An Elemental.

451
00:51:53.709 --> 00:51:57.304
Here.
One of the captives.

452
00:51:57.380 --> 00:52:00.315
And why, after 30 years,

453
00:52:00.383 --> 00:52:02.613
should it be you?

454
00:52:02.685 --> 00:52:05.085
He doesn't regard her
as a captive, though.

455
00:52:05.154 --> 00:52:07.952
Elementals...
they talk of neutrality,

456
00:52:08.024 --> 00:52:10.015
but they're all witches
and spies.

457
00:52:10.092 --> 00:52:13.027
Why else would they
come and go like the wind?

458
00:52:13.095 --> 00:52:17.122
But where has he gone?
Where is the Furyan hiding now?

459
00:52:17.199 --> 00:52:20.134
You be the good warrior.

460
00:52:20.202 --> 00:52:23.103
Go after this Riddick.

461
00:52:23.172 --> 00:52:26.801
I'll find out why the Lord Marshal
is so threatened by him.

462
00:53:26.102 --> 00:53:30.038
Do you know you
grind your teeth at night?

463
00:53:31.841 --> 00:53:33.570
Sexy.

464
00:53:49.792 --> 00:53:52.226
Destination reached.

465
00:53:52.294 --> 00:53:54.228
Unlocking manual controls.

466
00:53:54.296 --> 00:53:57.663
All right. I make 700 degrees
on the day side,

467
00:53:57.733 --> 00:53:59.701
300 below on the night side.

468
00:53:59.769 --> 00:54:02.738
Let's not get caught in the sun.

469
00:54:02.805 --> 00:54:05.239
If I owned this place and hell,

470
00:54:05.307 --> 00:54:08.299
I'd rent this place out
and live in hell.

471
00:54:17.053 --> 00:54:19.453
- Blue angle... good.
- Stand by.

472
00:54:20.956 --> 00:54:22.947
And...

473
00:54:23.025 --> 00:54:24.959
Plotted course good.

474
00:54:25.027 --> 00:54:27.427
Hit it!

475
00:54:27.496 --> 00:54:31.330
Angle of approach, not good.

476
00:54:38.674 --> 00:54:41.370
Look, Ma. No hands!

477
00:55:15.811 --> 00:55:17.745
Party poppers!

478
00:55:40.169 --> 00:55:42.535
I think I shit myself.

479
00:55:43.772 --> 00:55:46.935
Skittish, Toombs. Very skittish.

480
00:56:08.464 --> 00:56:10.398
Comfy?

481
00:56:27.850 --> 00:56:31.217
When the ride's over,

482
00:56:31.287 --> 00:56:33.847
your goggles are mine.

483
00:57:02.418 --> 00:57:05.478
Four-way split!

484
00:57:15.798 --> 00:57:18.096
29.4 kilometers.

485
00:57:26.609 --> 00:57:30.943
So, this is Riddick.

486
00:57:55.604 --> 00:57:59.631
What in the bowels of Christ
are you talkin' about, 700K?

487
00:57:59.708 --> 00:58:01.608
Don't take this one, boss.

488
00:58:01.677 --> 00:58:04.976
See? Anatoli here
has a nose for trouble.

489
00:58:05.047 --> 00:58:07.413
And this one, this Riddick guy...

490
00:58:07.483 --> 00:58:09.576
Big, big trouble.

491
00:58:09.652 --> 00:58:12.780
So, 700,000 is good money.

492
00:58:12.855 --> 00:58:16.621
I'd take the money, Toombs.

493
00:58:24.333 --> 00:58:28.861
The guild pays us a caretaker's
fee for each prisoner each year.

494
00:58:28.937 --> 00:58:32.964
We pay mercs 20% of that total fee
based on a certain life expectancy.

495
00:58:33.042 --> 00:58:34.669
How's about this?

496
00:58:34.743 --> 00:58:37.678
You open that safe you got hidden
behind the console there,

497
00:58:37.746 --> 00:58:41.876
show me the real books,
then we figure out my cut.

498
00:58:41.950 --> 00:58:43.941
Then I'll be on my way.

499
00:58:48.824 --> 00:58:52.191
Open my books.
This is what you suggest?

500
00:58:57.232 --> 00:58:59.223
Wasn't a suggestion.

501
00:59:17.086 --> 00:59:21.819
These are dangerous days,
if you believe the talk.

502
00:59:22.825 --> 00:59:25.851
Talk?
About dead planets.

503
00:59:25.928 --> 00:59:29.056
About some ghost army.

504
00:59:29.131 --> 00:59:31.793
About them.

505
00:59:31.867 --> 00:59:35.303
"Them"?

506
00:59:52.087 --> 00:59:54.021
I'll run the numbers again.

507
00:59:54.089 --> 00:59:56.182
It takes a couple of days,
probably,

508
00:59:56.258 --> 00:59:59.659
so you can stay as my guest.

509
00:59:59.728 --> 01:00:01.662
At least here, we are all safe.

510
01:00:01.730 --> 01:00:05.029
Yes? Yes, boss.

511
01:00:05.100 --> 01:00:07.500
I'll give it a day.

512
01:00:09.838 --> 01:00:11.965
One.

513
01:00:50.412 --> 01:00:52.346
There are inmates...

514
01:00:52.414 --> 01:00:55.144
and there are convicts.

515
01:00:55.217 --> 01:00:58.675
A convict has a certain code.

516
01:00:58.754 --> 01:01:02.690
And he knows to show
a certain respect.

517
01:01:03.759 --> 01:01:06.284
An inmate, on the other hand,

518
01:01:06.361 --> 01:01:08.886
pulls the pin on his fellow man.

519
01:01:08.964 --> 01:01:11.364
Does the guards’ work for them.

520
01:01:11.433 --> 01:01:14.027
Brings shame...

521
01:01:14.102 --> 01:01:16.468
to the game.

522
01:01:18.474 --> 01:01:21.443
So, which are you gonna be?

523
01:01:21.510 --> 01:01:24.035
Me?

524
01:01:26.148 --> 01:01:28.446
I'm just passin' through.

525
01:01:34.256 --> 01:01:36.417
Welcome to Crematoria.

526
01:01:42.598 --> 01:01:45.032
Should I go for the sweet spot?

527
01:01:45.100 --> 01:01:48.729
Left of the spine, fourth lumbar down,
the abdominal aorta.

528
01:01:48.804 --> 01:01:51.204
What a gusher.

529
01:01:53.542 --> 01:01:55.533
How do I get eyes like that?

530
01:01:55.611 --> 01:01:57.977
You gotta kill a few people.

531
01:01:58.046 --> 01:02:00.207
Did that.

532
01:02:00.282 --> 01:02:02.113
Did a lot of that.

533
01:02:03.719 --> 01:02:07.485
And then you gotta get sent to a slam. One where
they tell you you'll never see daylight again?

534
01:02:07.556 --> 01:02:11.151
Only there wasn't any doctor here who could
shine my eyes, not even for 20 menthol Kools.

535
01:02:11.226 --> 01:02:13.319
Was there anything
you said that was true?

536
01:02:16.098 --> 01:02:19.329
What are you gonna do, huh?
Go for the sweet spot?

537
01:02:19.401 --> 01:02:22.768
Remember who
you're talkin' to, Jack.

538
01:02:24.506 --> 01:02:27.839
Jack's dead.
She was weak.

539
01:02:29.011 --> 01:02:31.479
She couldn't cut it.

540
01:02:44.626 --> 01:02:46.787
The name's Kyra now.

541
01:02:46.862 --> 01:02:48.830
And I'm a new animal.

542
01:03:25.100 --> 01:03:29.764
They can be quite a test,
these deep runs...

543
01:03:31.607 --> 01:03:33.768
tests of our inner selves.

544
01:03:36.111 --> 01:03:38.477
Don't you find that true?

545
01:03:42.451 --> 01:03:44.476
Some men do.

546
01:03:45.887 --> 01:03:48.412
Just being so far from the armada,

547
01:03:48.490 --> 01:03:54.360
the mind can start to fill
with strange thoughts, doubts.

548
01:03:54.429 --> 01:03:57.364
Don't you ever have doubts, Vaako?

549
01:04:00.802 --> 01:04:03.293
- Doubts?
- About the campaign.

550
01:04:04.306 --> 01:04:06.467
About Lord Marshal.

551
01:04:08.477 --> 01:04:12.846
First and always,
I am a Necromonger commander.

552
01:04:13.915 --> 01:04:19.012
So if you're here to test my loyalty,
you succeed only in testing my patience.

553
01:04:19.087 --> 01:04:22.682
Oh, no.
No, that's not why I'm here at all.

554
01:04:44.112 --> 01:04:46.808
I'm so glad I could
steal you away for a moment.

555
01:04:46.882 --> 01:04:49.282
Doesn't it strike you odd?

556
01:04:49.351 --> 01:04:51.979
Here we have
the current Lord Marshal...

557
01:04:52.054 --> 01:04:56.150
destroying entire societies,
and yet he can't bring himself...

558
01:04:56.224 --> 01:05:00.183
to kill one stranded Elemental.

559
01:05:00.262 --> 01:05:02.196
Why is that?

560
01:05:03.398 --> 01:05:05.332
You don't pray to our god.

561
01:05:05.400 --> 01:05:07.960
You pray to no god, I hear.

562
01:05:08.036 --> 01:05:11.028
Elementals... we calculate.

563
01:05:12.107 --> 01:05:14.041
Don't we all.

564
01:05:14.109 --> 01:05:18.011
But now let's have first things first.

565
01:05:18.080 --> 01:05:21.311
What of Riddick? In truth, I
don't know where he went.

566
01:05:21.383 --> 01:05:24.318
In truth, I'm more interested
in where he came from.

567
01:05:26.455 --> 01:05:28.685
Watch your step.

568
01:05:28.757 --> 01:05:31.453
I've always wondered,

569
01:05:31.526 --> 01:05:34.120
does an air Elemental fly?

570
01:05:34.196 --> 01:05:36.187
Now do me a favor.

571
01:05:36.264 --> 01:05:40.223
Calculate the odds of you
getting off this planet alive...

572
01:05:40.302 --> 01:05:42.293
and now cut them in half.

573
01:05:43.739 --> 01:05:45.673
No, we can't fly.

574
01:05:45.741 --> 01:05:48.209
But we glide very well.

575
01:05:48.276 --> 01:05:51.074
Save your threats, Necromonger.

576
01:05:52.147 --> 01:05:55.708
I would have told you about Riddick
for the asking.

577
01:05:55.784 --> 01:05:59.584
It concerns a foretelling,
a prediction now more than 30 years old.

578
01:05:59.654 --> 01:06:03.954
A young warrior
once consulted a seer.

579
01:06:04.025 --> 01:06:09.088
He was told a child would be born
on the planet Furya... a male child...

580
01:06:09.164 --> 01:06:13.567
who would someday
cause the warrior's downfall.

581
01:06:13.635 --> 01:06:17.230
Cause his untimed death.

582
01:06:18.240 --> 01:06:23.200
Furya? Furya's a ruined world.
No life to speak of.

583
01:06:23.278 --> 01:06:24.836
For good reason.

584
01:06:24.913 --> 01:06:29.907
This young warrior
mounted an attack on Furya,

585
01:06:29.985 --> 01:06:33.079
killing all young males
he could find,

586
01:06:33.155 --> 01:06:37.251
even strangling some
with their birth cords.

587
01:06:37.325 --> 01:06:40.123
An artful stroke,
wouldn't you say?

588
01:06:42.030 --> 01:06:46.057
So this warrior, the one who tried to outwit
the prediction, would later become...

589
01:06:46.134 --> 01:06:48.159
That's why he worries.

590
01:06:48.236 --> 01:06:50.227
The Lord Marshal.

591
01:06:51.840 --> 01:06:53.831
Which would make
the man-child...

592
01:06:53.909 --> 01:06:56.377
He worries he missed
killing that child in its crib.

593
01:06:56.444 --> 01:06:58.435
Riddick.

594
01:07:15.463 --> 01:07:17.624
That's why it's so vital to him.
Wait.

595
01:07:17.699 --> 01:07:20.099
- It's about a prophecy.
- Wait! Wait!

596
01:07:23.138 --> 01:07:25.129
Are you there?

597
01:07:28.677 --> 01:07:31.077
You do what your lord asks.

598
01:07:31.146 --> 01:07:34.809
You cleanse Riddick for him,
and in doing so...

599
01:07:34.883 --> 01:07:38.284
you prove your undying loyalty.

600
01:07:38.353 --> 01:07:43.985
And perhaps then
he'll finally let down his guard.

601
01:08:26.768 --> 01:08:28.292
Still here, I see?

602
01:08:28.370 --> 01:08:32.101
I've been here 18 years.
See this?

603
01:08:34.175 --> 01:08:40.011
I remember how gorgeous she was.
Well, gorgeous in a certain light.

604
01:08:40.081 --> 01:08:42.982
And now,
for the goddamn death of me,

605
01:08:43.051 --> 01:08:45.178
I cannot remember her name.

606
01:08:45.387 --> 01:08:47.821
Feeding time!

607
01:08:52.193 --> 01:08:56.186
We're here for the rest
of our unnatural lives.

608
01:09:04.205 --> 01:09:05.900
Here they come!

609
01:09:11.212 --> 01:09:15.080
Whatever you do,
don't make eye contact.

610
01:10:14.242 --> 01:10:15.732
Aaah!

611
01:11:40.829 --> 01:11:42.820
It's an animal thing.

612
01:11:53.741 --> 01:11:57.336
Check her for me.
She's always got a blade somewhere.

613
01:12:24.072 --> 01:12:27.371
Hyah!

614
01:12:57.105 --> 01:13:00.097
I don't think
she likes being touched.

615
01:13:02.277 --> 01:13:06.577
I'd take my wounded and go
while you still can.

616
01:13:12.053 --> 01:13:16.114
Is there a name for this
private little world of yours, huh?

617
01:13:16.191 --> 01:13:20.992
What happens there
when we don't just run away?

618
01:13:21.062 --> 01:13:23.530
You'll kill us... with a soup cup?

619
01:13:23.598 --> 01:13:25.930
Tea, actually.

620
01:13:26.000 --> 01:13:27.934
What's that?

621
01:13:30.505 --> 01:13:33.997
I'll kill you with my teacup.

622
01:13:45.753 --> 01:13:49.086
You know the rule. They aren't dead
if they're still on the books.

623
01:13:49.157 --> 01:13:52.320
Mmm.

624
01:14:09.777 --> 01:14:11.267
Come on.

625
01:14:34.135 --> 01:14:36.228
Death by teacup.

626
01:14:40.408 --> 01:14:42.842
Damn. Why didn't I think of that?

627
01:14:42.910 --> 01:14:45.743
I didn't come to play
"Who's the Better Killer?"

628
01:14:45.813 --> 01:14:49.214
But it's my favorite game.
Haven't you heard?

629
01:14:49.284 --> 01:14:51.718
I heard you came lookin' for me.
Is that all?

630
01:14:51.786 --> 01:14:54.448
Then you missed the good part.

631
01:14:54.522 --> 01:14:56.786
Hooked up with some mercs
outta Lupus Five.

632
01:14:56.858 --> 01:15:00.225
Said they'd take me on,
teach me the trade, give me a good cut.

633
01:15:01.529 --> 01:15:03.156
They slaved me out, Riddick.

634
01:15:03.231 --> 01:15:06.359
Do you know what that could do to you
when you're that age?

635
01:15:06.434 --> 01:15:10.029
When you're 12 years old?
I told you to stay in New Mecca.

636
01:15:10.104 --> 01:15:12.629
Did you not listen?

637
01:15:12.707 --> 01:15:14.902
I had mercs on my neck.

638
01:15:14.976 --> 01:15:17.410
I'll always have mercs on my neck.

639
01:15:17.478 --> 01:15:21.141
I spent five years on a frozen heap
just to keep 'em away from you.

640
01:15:22.150 --> 01:15:25.085
And you go and sign up
with the same fake badges...

641
01:15:25.153 --> 01:15:27.144
that wanted to cut you up
and use you for bait.

642
01:15:27.221 --> 01:15:31.590
What are you pitching, Riddick?
That you cuttin' out was a good thing?

643
01:15:31.659 --> 01:15:35.095
That you had my ass covered
from halfway across the universe?

644
01:15:35.163 --> 01:15:37.757
You signed with mercs.

645
01:15:41.502 --> 01:15:44.335
There was nobody else around.

646
01:15:58.286 --> 01:16:01.414
Let's pop the cork.
Get some fresh air.

647
01:16:38.526 --> 01:16:40.619
So they do go topside...

648
01:16:42.029 --> 01:16:44.793
to swap out air.

649
01:16:44.866 --> 01:16:47.300
Interesting.

650
01:16:47.368 --> 01:16:49.097
Who the hell are you?

651
01:16:51.038 --> 01:16:54.439
When it happens, it'll happen fast.

652
01:16:54.509 --> 01:16:57.945
Stay on my leg when I cut fence
or stay here...

653
01:16:58.012 --> 01:17:00.003
for the rest of your natural life.

654
01:17:00.081 --> 01:17:03.949
Nobody outs this place.
Nobody.

655
01:17:09.991 --> 01:17:12.323
He ain't "nobody."

656
01:17:26.374 --> 01:17:30.743
Good news first.
Talked things over with my amigos here.

657
01:17:30.812 --> 01:17:34.043
We'll cut you in for 775K.

658
01:17:36.484 --> 01:17:38.543
Well, all right.

659
01:17:38.619 --> 01:17:40.985
What's the bad news?
They close the local whorehouse?

660
01:17:43.658 --> 01:17:47.424
No. The bad news is worse than that.
Much worse.

661
01:17:47.495 --> 01:17:52.523
Our pilot, he saw this.
It crossed a shipping lane.

662
01:17:56.070 --> 01:17:59.562
Any idea what this might be?

663
01:18:03.177 --> 01:18:06.169
Never saw nothin' like it.

664
01:18:06.247 --> 01:18:09.944
This ship charts back
to Helion Prime.

665
01:18:10.017 --> 01:18:13.544
You know, Anatoli's
got a nose for trouble,

666
01:18:13.621 --> 01:18:17.682
and he thinks
trouble follows you here.

667
01:18:19.794 --> 01:18:24.128
Look. We dusted our tracks
and got the hell outta there.

668
01:18:24.198 --> 01:18:27.190
There is no way
we didn't lose them.

669
01:18:28.336 --> 01:18:31.237
"Them"?

670
01:18:36.677 --> 01:18:39.908
This is my prisoner. Mine.

671
01:18:39.981 --> 01:18:41.972
Nobody else's.

672
01:18:42.049 --> 01:18:44.381
And I want my money now.

673
01:18:44.452 --> 01:18:46.545
So...

674
01:18:46.621 --> 01:18:49.055
you stole a prisoner...

675
01:18:49.123 --> 01:18:51.114
from "them"?

676
01:19:58.359 --> 01:20:00.554
No.

677
01:20:00.628 --> 01:20:03.722
Riddick. No!

678
01:20:08.936 --> 01:20:12.929
Shoulda taken the money, Toombs.

679
01:21:08.896 --> 01:21:11.421
You gonna kill me?

680
01:21:44.765 --> 01:21:46.960
Mercs.

681
01:21:48.436 --> 01:21:50.870
Some guards here,
but this can't be all of them.

682
01:21:52.106 --> 01:21:55.405
Check their slots in the back...
and be careful.

683
01:21:55.476 --> 01:21:57.467
Don't bother.

684
01:21:57.545 --> 01:21:59.945
Guards ain't there.

685
01:22:00.014 --> 01:22:02.744
They figured out the Necros
are comin' for me.

686
01:22:02.817 --> 01:22:05.980
Plan was to clean the bank,
ghost the mercs,

687
01:22:06.053 --> 01:22:07.987
break wide through the tunnel.

688
01:22:08.055 --> 01:22:11.786
And then somebody got a lucky shot off
with this rocket launcher here...

689
01:22:11.859 --> 01:22:13.850
and took out the sled.

690
01:22:13.928 --> 01:22:18.058
Guards took off on foot but rigged
the door so no one could follow.

691
01:22:19.133 --> 01:22:23.729
They'll take the one ship in the hangar
and leave everyone else here to die.

692
01:22:23.804 --> 01:22:27.171
How come you know all this shit?

693
01:22:27.241 --> 01:22:29.266
You weren't even here.

694
01:22:30.277 --> 01:22:32.404
'Cause it was my plan.

695
01:22:38.119 --> 01:22:40.679
I shoulda taken the money.

696
01:22:47.428 --> 01:22:49.658
Riddick!

697
01:23:00.241 --> 01:23:03.369
What is this?
What is he thinking?

698
01:23:03.444 --> 01:23:06.413
- Once that sun comes up...
- We'll last five minutes.

699
01:23:06.480 --> 01:23:10.439
Five minutes. We ain't gonna last
30 seconds out there.

700
01:23:10.518 --> 01:23:12.509
It'll light you up like a match.

701
01:23:17.091 --> 01:23:21.255
20-mile buffer zone
and 30 klicks to the hangar.

702
01:23:23.430 --> 01:23:26.695
30 klicks over that terrain?

703
01:23:39.213 --> 01:23:43.377
It's moving in the right direction.
We could make it.

704
01:23:43.751 --> 01:23:46.447
Stay behind the night,

705
01:23:46.520 --> 01:23:48.818
ahead of the sun.

706
01:23:48.889 --> 01:23:51.221
There's gonna be one speed...

707
01:23:53.327 --> 01:23:55.318
mine.

708
01:23:57.598 --> 01:23:59.759
If you can't keep up, don't step up.

709
01:23:59.834 --> 01:24:01.768
You'll just die.

710
01:25:05.900 --> 01:25:07.663
Riddick?

711
01:25:09.737 --> 01:25:11.728
Riddick?

712
01:25:15.109 --> 01:25:17.100
Riddick?

713
01:25:21.615 --> 01:25:25.142
Go, go! Go on! Go! Climb here!

714
01:25:25.219 --> 01:25:27.881
Climb! Go! Go, go, go!

715
01:25:53.580 --> 01:25:55.411
Boss!

716
01:25:59.253 --> 01:26:01.221
Up there.

717
01:26:01.288 --> 01:26:03.483
- Take a look.
- Because Anatoli says so?

718
01:26:03.557 --> 01:26:06.651
Because his nose says so.

719
01:26:23.944 --> 01:26:26.504
There's nothin' up here.

720
01:26:28.582 --> 01:26:30.015
Oh, shit.

721
01:26:39.793 --> 01:26:42.353
Riddick.

722
01:26:42.429 --> 01:26:46.058
They're heading right for the volcano fields.
They're going for our ship!

723
01:26:46.133 --> 01:26:48.727
No chance do they get to the
hangar first. No chance!

724
01:27:00.514 --> 01:27:02.709
Next one! Next hole!
We'll catch 'em there!

725
01:27:30.644 --> 01:27:32.942
No more run for you.

726
01:27:38.152 --> 01:27:41.588
Where did the big guy go?

727
01:27:47.327 --> 01:27:49.295
Ohh...

728
01:28:14.354 --> 01:28:16.083
Close it!

729
01:28:47.688 --> 01:28:50.521
What was that?
You don't care if you live or die?

730
01:28:50.591 --> 01:28:53.617
If I kill them first, not really.

731
01:28:55.262 --> 01:28:57.355
Maybe I do.

732
01:28:57.431 --> 01:28:59.422
Keep moving!

733
01:29:56.757 --> 01:29:59.851
Kyra?

734
01:29:59.927 --> 01:30:01.952
- Kyra!
- What?

735
01:30:02.029 --> 01:30:04.691
Get that ass moving!

736
01:30:42.369 --> 01:30:45.236
Riddick?

737
01:30:49.910 --> 01:30:53.903
Remember what I said
about not caring if I lived or died?

738
01:30:57.584 --> 01:30:59.779
You knew I was kidding, right?

739
01:31:03.056 --> 01:31:04.546
"One speed."

740
01:31:25.178 --> 01:31:27.043
Temperature differential.

741
01:31:27.114 --> 01:31:29.605
Your rope.

742
01:31:29.683 --> 01:31:32.049
It's too late.
We're never gonna make it.

743
01:31:32.119 --> 01:31:34.212
Your rope! Gimme your rope!

744
01:31:35.355 --> 01:31:37.414
And your water. All of it!

745
01:31:38.458 --> 01:31:41.916
Stay in the shadow of the mountain.
Don't wait for me. Run!

746
01:31:53.840 --> 01:31:56.206
Riddick!

747
01:32:07.254 --> 01:32:08.653
Aaah!

748
01:32:40.153 --> 01:32:42.087
Where the hell is that hangar?

749
01:32:47.094 --> 01:32:50.894
There it is.

750
01:32:52.899 --> 01:32:53.399
Listen.

751
01:33:22.496 --> 01:33:25.431
Let me guess. Necros.

752
01:33:25.499 --> 01:33:28.696
And a whole lotta Necro firepower.

753
01:33:28.769 --> 01:33:32.068
Shit! I hate not being the bad guys.

754
01:34:00.133 --> 01:34:05.264
I figure we got three minutes before the sun
hits us again, burns out this whole valley.

755
01:34:05.338 --> 01:34:08.034
- Wait.
- We gonna do this or not?

756
01:34:08.108 --> 01:34:10.008
Just wait.

757
01:34:15.081 --> 01:34:17.242
Ellen.

758
01:34:18.685 --> 01:34:21.654
Her name was Ellen.
I never really forgot.

759
01:34:38.939 --> 01:34:41.533
Aaah! Boss!

760
01:34:52.786 --> 01:34:56.654
- Remember that favorite game of yours?
- "Who's the Better Killer?"

761
01:34:58.792 --> 01:35:02.785
- Let's play.
- Come on!

762
01:35:21.081 --> 01:35:22.776
On the right!

763
01:35:30.290 --> 01:35:32.087
Watch out!
Behind you!

764
01:35:32.158 --> 01:35:33.921
Kyra!

765
01:36:29.983 --> 01:36:32.008
Sybar!

766
01:37:33.546 --> 01:37:35.480
No!

767
01:37:57.504 --> 01:37:59.734
Aaah!

768
01:38:17.424 --> 01:38:20.120
Get up. Get up!

769
01:38:20.193 --> 01:38:22.161
Please get up.

770
01:38:35.475 --> 01:38:37.136
So,

771
01:38:39.045 --> 01:38:41.843
you can kneel.

772
01:38:59.299 --> 01:39:01.790
I think you know now.

773
01:39:03.470 --> 01:39:05.904
I think you know
who tore Furya apart.

774
01:39:09.242 --> 01:39:12.769
This mark carries the anger
of an entire race.

775
01:39:18.118 --> 01:39:20.211
But it's going to hurt.

776
01:41:38.057 --> 01:41:40.287
Kyra?

777
01:41:44.163 --> 01:41:47.098
I was supposed to
deliver a message to you...

778
01:41:49.068 --> 01:41:51.366
if Vaako failed to kill you.

779
01:41:53.273 --> 01:41:56.037
A message from
the Lord Marshal himself.

780
01:41:57.944 --> 01:42:01.436
He tells you to stay away from Helion,
stay away from him,

781
01:42:02.782 --> 01:42:04.909
and in return,
you'll be hunted no more.

782
01:42:11.891 --> 01:42:14.724
But Vaako will most likely
report you as dead.

783
01:42:16.129 --> 01:42:18.393
So this is your chance.

784
01:42:18.464 --> 01:42:22.230
Your chance to do
what no man has ever done.

785
01:42:22.302 --> 01:42:24.293
The girl.

786
01:42:25.305 --> 01:42:27.500
Where will they take her?

787
01:42:44.490 --> 01:42:47.823
We all began... as something else.

788
01:42:52.065 --> 01:42:56.661
I've done... unbelievable things...

789
01:42:57.670 --> 01:43:00.434
in the name of a faith
that was never my own.

790
01:43:02.342 --> 01:43:06.301
And he'll do to her
what he did to me.

791
01:43:12.552 --> 01:43:17.182
The Necromonger in me
warns you not to go back.

792
01:43:18.524 --> 01:43:21.152
But the Furyan in me...

793
01:43:24.697 --> 01:43:26.426
hopes you won't listen.

794
01:43:32.271 --> 01:43:36.935
God knows... I've dreamed of it.

795
01:44:38.137 --> 01:44:41.004
I have lost a Purifier...

796
01:44:42.241 --> 01:44:47.042
but I have gained
a first among commanders.

797
01:44:48.047 --> 01:44:50.675
It is overdue, isn't it...

798
01:44:50.750 --> 01:44:53.446
that we acknowledge
your many accomplishments,

799
01:44:53.519 --> 01:44:55.680
your steady faith,

800
01:44:55.755 --> 01:45:01.284
and above all,
your unflinching loyalty.

801
01:45:09.035 --> 01:45:12.527
Obedience without question.
Loyalty till UnderVerse come.

802
01:45:15.041 --> 01:45:17.032
Well done, Vaako.

803
01:45:18.311 --> 01:45:21.906
This is a day of days.

804
01:45:41.701 --> 01:45:44.226
Look more pleased, Vaako.

805
01:45:46.005 --> 01:45:49.406
You have killed his enemy...

806
01:45:49.475 --> 01:45:51.238
and his suspicions.

807
01:45:51.310 --> 01:45:56.111
- I should have brought back his head.
- You saw him unbreathing. You saw him dead on the ground.

808
01:45:56.182 --> 01:45:59.174
Riddick was no common breeder.
In a heartbeat he dropped 20 of my men.

809
01:45:59.252 --> 01:46:03.211
All mysteries are not miracles,
not even in this religion.

810
01:46:05.725 --> 01:46:08.319
And if you say it is certain,
then it is certain,

811
01:46:08.394 --> 01:46:11.693
and we've already said it,
haven't we?

812
01:46:14.333 --> 01:46:16.324
We have.

813
01:46:20.106 --> 01:46:22.631
Now, tell me if it's true.

814
01:46:22.708 --> 01:46:26.940
Tell me the Furyan is gone, and I can close
this campaign without hearing his bootsteps.

815
01:46:28.447 --> 01:46:30.438
If he is dead,

816
01:46:31.617 --> 01:46:33.642
I sense I'm not far
from the same fate,

817
01:46:34.720 --> 01:46:36.654
being of no further use here.

818
01:46:37.723 --> 01:46:40.783
Shouldn't I tell you
that Riddick is still alive?

819
01:46:40.860 --> 01:46:42.657
Don't try me, Aereon.

820
01:46:42.728 --> 01:46:44.992
I could plow you under
with the rest of Helion Prime.

821
01:46:45.064 --> 01:46:47.396
No one really knows the future.

822
01:46:47.466 --> 01:46:51.266
Then tell me the odds
that Vaako met with success,

823
01:46:51.337 --> 01:46:53.328
that I will now be the one...

824
01:46:53.406 --> 01:46:56.307
who can carry his people across
the threshold into UnderVerse,

825
01:46:56.375 --> 01:46:58.366
where they shall begin true life.

826
01:46:58.444 --> 01:47:00.742
Tell me what I want to hear, Aereon,

827
01:47:00.813 --> 01:47:04.909
and maybe
I'll save your home world... for last.

828
01:47:09.755 --> 01:47:12.246
- The odds are good...
- That?

829
01:47:12.325 --> 01:47:14.885
That you will reach the UnderVerse...

830
01:47:18.097 --> 01:47:20.088
soon.

831
01:47:58.471 --> 01:48:00.268
Ascension protocol!

832
01:48:00.339 --> 01:48:04.036
We still have numbers out there, Lord Marshal...
sweep teams, recon ships.

833
01:48:04.110 --> 01:48:06.169
They would be hard-pressed
to make it back...

834
01:48:10.983 --> 01:48:14.783
Get my armada off the ground!

835
01:49:16.315 --> 01:49:19.876
- You mean on Helion?
- I mean here, on this very ship!

836
01:49:19.952 --> 01:49:24.252
Could you be wrong?
Mind fabricates fear.

837
01:49:24.323 --> 01:49:28.589
Could you be wrong? Not so wrong
as you when you left him alive!

838
01:49:28.661 --> 01:49:30.595
It's twice a mistake.

839
01:49:30.663 --> 01:49:33.928
Not only your failure,
but now the report of success.

840
01:49:33.999 --> 01:49:37.594
How do we salvage this? How? How?

841
01:49:37.670 --> 01:49:40.230
Lord Marshal's got to be warned.

842
01:49:40.306 --> 01:49:42.240
You will never see the UnderVerse!

843
01:49:43.576 --> 01:49:45.703
He will kill us both
before our due time.

844
01:49:48.848 --> 01:49:50.782
I say give Riddick his chance.

845
01:49:55.621 --> 01:49:58.215
If he is half of what you think,

846
01:49:58.290 --> 01:50:00.315
he can at least wound the Lord Marshal...

847
01:50:00.393 --> 01:50:02.884
and that is when you must act.

848
01:50:02.962 --> 01:50:05.328
Just to take his place?
Just to keep what I kill?

849
01:50:05.398 --> 01:50:08.128
- That is the Necromonger way.
- It is not enough!

850
01:50:08.200 --> 01:50:10.964
Then you do it for the faith!

851
01:50:11.036 --> 01:50:13.766
If he has fear, he has weakness.

852
01:50:13.839 --> 01:50:15.773
If he has weakness, Vaako...

853
01:50:17.810 --> 01:50:19.971
He is unworthy of lordship.

854
01:50:20.980 --> 01:50:23.312
We do it for all Necromongers.

855
01:50:24.817 --> 01:50:26.978
Protect the faith.

856
01:50:27.052 --> 01:50:30.078
This can still be a day of days,

857
01:50:30.156 --> 01:50:32.249
but the timing...

858
01:50:32.324 --> 01:50:35.316
must be flawless.

859
01:50:57.149 --> 01:51:00.676
Final protocol.
Execute on my order.

860
01:51:35.588 --> 01:51:37.852
Go inside.

861
01:51:38.958 --> 01:51:40.949
Are they leaving now?

862
01:51:41.026 --> 01:51:43.790
Ziza! Go inside!

863
01:52:35.548 --> 01:52:37.812
We found this Lensor dead.

864
01:52:40.386 --> 01:52:43.844
Show me his last sight.

865
01:52:56.235 --> 01:52:57.930
Commander Toal.

866
01:52:58.003 --> 01:52:59.994
He won't escape twice.

867
01:54:52.384 --> 01:54:55.512
Stay your weapons!

868
01:54:56.955 --> 01:54:58.946
He came for me.

869
01:55:25.718 --> 01:55:28.084
Consider this:

870
01:55:32.958 --> 01:55:37.054
If you fall here now,

871
01:55:37.129 --> 01:55:39.063
you'll never rise.

872
01:55:39.131 --> 01:55:42.259
But if you choose another way...

873
01:55:43.435 --> 01:55:45.596
the Necromonger way...

874
01:55:45.671 --> 01:55:48.196
you'll die in due time...

875
01:55:48.273 --> 01:55:52.004
and rise again in the UnderVerse.

876
01:56:01.653 --> 01:56:03.848
Go to him.

877
01:56:11.363 --> 01:56:13.354
It hurts...

878
01:56:14.366 --> 01:56:16.630
at first.

879
01:56:16.702 --> 01:56:20.297
But after a while, the pain goes
away, just as they promise.

880
01:56:22.708 --> 01:56:25.233
- Are you with me, Kyra?
- There's a moment...

881
01:56:25.310 --> 01:56:27.710
when you can almost
see the UnderVerse through his eyes.

882
01:56:29.047 --> 01:56:31.811
It makes it sound perfect...

883
01:56:31.884 --> 01:56:33.818
a place where anyone
can start over.

884
01:56:33.886 --> 01:56:36.354
Are you with me, Kyra?

885
01:56:48.901 --> 01:56:51.335
Convert now...

886
01:56:51.403 --> 01:56:53.564
or fall forever.

887
01:56:58.343 --> 01:57:00.607
You killed everything I know.

888
01:57:05.751 --> 01:57:06.945
Vaako.

889
01:57:09.054 --> 01:57:11.318
Not yet.

890
01:57:22.868 --> 01:57:25.837
Been a long time
since I've seen my own blood.

891
01:58:44.116 --> 01:58:47.108
These are his last moments.

892
01:59:06.705 --> 01:59:09.538
Give me your soul.

893
01:59:14.546 --> 01:59:17.982
Fuck you!

894
02:00:23.281 --> 02:00:25.545
You're not the one to bring me down.

895
02:00:44.536 --> 02:00:47.266
Now! Kill the beast
while he's wounded!

896
02:01:04.956 --> 02:01:07.982
Help me, Vaako. Kill him.

897
02:01:15.634 --> 02:01:16.965
Vaako?

898
02:01:21.640 --> 02:01:23.631
Forgive me.

899
02:01:23.708 --> 02:01:25.403
Flawless.

900
02:01:56.274 --> 02:01:58.742
No.

901
02:02:04.816 --> 02:02:08.217
No-o-o!

902
02:02:08.286 --> 02:02:11.380
Now what would be
the odds of that?

903
02:02:24.369 --> 02:02:26.963
I thought you were dead.

904
02:02:29.207 --> 02:02:31.767
Are you with me, Kyra?

905
02:02:33.845 --> 02:02:36.405
I was always with you.

906
02:02:38.750 --> 02:02:40.741
I was.

907
02:04:04.302 --> 02:04:06.634
You keep what you kill.
